    "body": "## What does this implement/fix?\r\n\r\n| Property | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Method | `onReceive` |\r\n| Class | `com.craxiom.networksurvey.SimChangeReceiver` |\r\n| File | `networksurvey/src/main/java/com/craxiom/networksurvey/SimChangeReceiver.java` |\r\n| Specification | `DeprecatedLibrarySpec` |\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\n### Reported finding\r\n\r\nThe finding (`DeprecatedLibrarySpec`) reported for `com.craxiom.networksurvey.SimChangeReceiver.onReceive`:\r\n\r\n> androidx.localbroadcastmanager.content.LocalBroadcastManager is deprecated. Use LiveData or reactive streams.\r\n\r\n### Root cause\r\n\r\nSimChangeReceiver.onReceive directly invokes the forbidden, fully deprecated androidx.localbroadcastmanager.content.LocalBroadcastManager API to emit SIM_CHANGED_INTENT; the same deprecated event channel is also used by three statically linked production consumers.\r\n\r\n### Correction strategy\r\n\r\nRetire AndroidX LocalBroadcastManager 1.1.0 and use the repository's existing LiveData idiom for the internal SIM_CHANGED_INTENT channel. Preserve the established sender guards and CONTRACT-defined main-thread deferred dispatch and unsubscription/cancellation invariants, while designing the observable publication so LiveData replay or postValue coalescing does not silently alter required event semantics.\r\n\r\n### Coordinated changes\r\n\r\n- `networksurvey/src/main/java/com/craxiom/networksurvey/SimChangeReceiver.java`: Removes LocalBroadcastManager and preserves guarded, deferred main-thread event delivery through LiveData. The synchronized sequence assignment and individually queued main-looper setValue calls preserve distinct accepted emissions, while the exposed sequence permits each migrated consumer to suppress replayed values and remove its retained observer during cleanup.\r\n- `networksurvey/src/main/java/com/craxiom/networksurvey/fragments/MainCellularFragment.java`: The fragment no longer creates a BroadcastReceiver after migrating its SIM-change subscription to the shared LiveData channel.; IntentFilter was only required by the removed LocalBroadcastManager registration.; The fragment now observes SimChangeReceiver's process-local LiveData channel rather than LocalBroadcastManager.; Retains the exact Observer instance required for explicit removeObserver cleanup and stores the sequence baseline used to suppress LiveData replay values predating this subscription.; Subscribes with a retained Observer<Long>, captures the sender-provided current sequence immediately before registration, and only forwards strictly newer events to the preserved public SIM-change handling entry point. observeForever preserves the prior registration-to-destruction delivery window while explicit removal below provides LocalBroadcastManager-equivalent cancellation.; Removes the exact retained LiveData Observer at the existing receiver cleanup point, preventing delivery of events that were queued before destruction but dispatched afterward.\r\n- `networksurvey/src/main/java/com/craxiom/networksurvey/fragments/TowerMapFragment.kt`: Removes obsolete BroadcastReceiver, Intent, IntentFilter, and LocalBroadcastManager imports and adds the retained AndroidX Lifecycle Observer type required by the shared LiveData subscription.; Replaces the LocalBroadcastManager receiver with a retained LiveData Observer. The observer preserves the existing tower-map reset reaction only for events newer than the baseline captured when this fragment subscribes.; Captures the shared event channel's current sequence immediately before registration, then subscribes the retained observer. Any replayed value at or below the captured baseline is filtered by the observer while later queued events retain the existing reaction.; Explicitly removes the exact retained LiveData observer at the fragment's existing cleanup point, preserving the prior guarantee that the fragment does not receive SIM-change events after unregistration.\r\n- `networksurvey/src/main/java/com/craxiom/networksurvey/services/controller/CellularController.java`: Remove the deprecated LocalBroadcastManager dependency from this consumer and import the retained Lifecycle LiveData observer type supplied by the coordinated dependency migration.; Retain the exact Observer<Long> instance so the controller can explicitly remove the same subscription during teardown.; Preserve explicit cancellation semantics by removing the retained observer at the existing teardown point; removal is independent of surveyService availability because the channel is process-local.; Keep the existing private registration entry-point name, capture the shared channel sequence immediately before subscription, and filter replayed values at or below that baseline. The retained observer converts accepted channel events into the original SIM-change Intent handling path, while the public onReceive(Context, Intent) method preserves the required handling entry point and applies the former IntentFilter action constraint.\r\n- `gradle/libs.versions.toml`: Replaces the obsolete LocalBroadcastManager-only version with the explicit AndroidX Lifecycle version required by the new direct Lifecycle LiveData dependency.; Removes the deprecated LocalBroadcastManager alias and provides the version-catalog alias that networksurvey/build.gradle will use for the shared LiveData event channel.\r\n- `networksurvey/build.gradle`: Remove the obsolete LocalBroadcastManager implementation dependency and provide AndroidX Lifecycle LiveData on the production classpath for SimChangeReceiver and its migrated consumers.\r\n- `networksurvey/src/test/java/com/craxiom/networksurvey/SimChangeEventSubscriptionTest.java`: Adds focused tests for the shared LiveData channel's monotonic sequence baseline contract. Each observer is retained and removed during cleanup, mirroring production cancellation requirements and avoiding cross-test subscriptions to the process-local channel.\r\n- `networksurvey/src/androidTest/java/com/craxiom/networksurvey/SimChangeLiveDataInstrumentationTest.java`: Adds instrumentation assertions for null and wrong-action guards, valid deferred main-looper delivery, replay suppression using the required subscription baseline, and retained-observer removal before both pending and subsequent events. These are the shared channel semantics required by the migrated fragment and controller consumers.\r\n\r\n\r\n## How was this tested?\r\n\r\n- [x] Automated test coverage added in 2 test file(s)\r\n- [x] Project compiles successfully (`:networksurvey:assembleCdrDebugAndroidTest :networksurvey:testCdrDebugUnitTest`)\r\n- [ ] Confirmed by a project maintainer\r\n\r\n## Additional context\r\n\r\nI’m an undergraduate Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), and this contribution is part of a research project involving static analysis of Android apps.\r\n\r\nI’m happy to adjust the implementation to better match the project’s architecture, coding conventions, or maintainers’ recommendations.",
